{"acceleration_structures":[],"air_sha256":"845f9a22882d20a197d79002adc2caa4269b9d5f356bcc0c659fc8ec4528f846","argument_buffer_buffers":[],"argument_buffer_intersection_function_tables":[],"argument_buffer_textures":[],"authored_by":"claude:opus-5","buffers":[{"binding":0,"bytes_b64":"AAAAPwCAyEIAwEhDABCWQwAAwD8AgMpCAMBJQwCQlkMAACBAAIDMQgDASkMAEJdDAABgQACAzkIAwEtDAJCXQwAAkEAAgNBCAMBMQwAQmEMAALBAAIDSQgDATUMAkJhDAADQQACA1EIAwE5DABCZQwAA8EAAgNZCAMBPQwCQmUM=","role":"input"},{"binding":1,"initial_bytes_b64":"q6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6s=","role":"output"}],"case_id":"ae41a7fb5893f03c64e1a5461087219d282594c727840af45f63b89559859eee","compare":{"kind":"exact"},"device_buffer_arrays":[],"dispatch":{"grid":[8,1,1],"threads_per_threadgroup":[8,1,1]},"entry":"kernel_byte_view_scalar_through_helper","execution_safety":"loop_free","function_constants":[],"intersection_function_tables":[],"kernel_stage_inputs":[],"name":"read-a-scalar-and-a-vector-through-one-byte-view","output":{"binding":1,"kind":"buffer","length":128,"offset":0},"rationale":"A device pointer parked in a struct field and read back by an OUT-OF-LINE helper, which is the shape that leaves the pointer a Private byte placeholder while the helper is emitted: the store that gave it an address is in the caller, so the byte-view loads have to be deferred and repaired after inlining. The helper reads a packed_float3 at +0 and a lone float at +12 from the same dynamic base, and both reach the emitter as scalar float loads through a uchar pointer. Before the fix this module could not be translated at all -- emit_scalar_slots_to_wider_load assembled a wider VECTOR result from narrow slots but declined a scalar one, and the load reported 'cannot reinterpret load of byte pointer to Float without a logical-pointer bitcast'; ten corpus sources failed on that asymmetry. The eight records hold distinct exactly-representable floats, so an assembly that reads the wrong bytes, or that reads Private scratch instead of the bound buffer, cannot reproduce the output.","render_targets":[],"samplers":[],"stage":"kernel","texture_arrays":[],"textures":[],"threadgroup_memory":[],"vertex_inputs":[],"visible_function_references":[],"visible_function_tables":[]}
{"acceleration_structures":[],"air_sha256":"84822625225c0536ed8dc9c33d49a6b872f313b5ea0909e4008342f87849b9cd","argument_buffer_buffers":[],"argument_buffer_intersection_function_tables":[],"argument_buffer_textures":[],"authored_by":"claude:opus-5","buffers":[{"binding":0,"bytes_b64":"AgA=","role":"input"}],"case_id":"f8494e2f69a6057e0c5ad94bfd1e40047861ef1b80d4c4c356696424ddc0d39f","compare":{"kind":"exact"},"device_buffer_arrays":[],"dispatch":{"grid":[2,1,1],"threads_per_threadgroup":[2,1,1]},"entry":"depthFilterSeparableSlidingStacks_array","execution_safety":"authored_bounded","function_constants":[],"intersection_function_tables":[],"kernel_stage_inputs":[],"name":"slide-a-five-layer-box-across-six-layers-with-both-edges-short","output":{"binding":1,"dimensions":[2,1,6],"kind":"texture","origin":[0,0,0]},"rationale":"No authored case reached `llvm.smin.i16`, which six corpus sources use; this 166-line kernel is the smallest and calls it exactly once, in the denominator of its running box average, so the call's answer is visible in every output texel. The kernel slides a (2*boxRadius + 1)-layer box along the array axis of a 2d texture array, keeping a running sum: at step t it subtracts layer t - 2r - 1 when that layer exists, adds layer t when it exists, and at t >= r divides by the number of layers actually inside the box. That count is `(2r + 1) + select(t < arraySize, 0, arraySize - 1 - t) + smin(t - 2r, 0)`: the select shortens the box at the trailing edge and the `smin` shortens it at the leading edge. With boxRadius 2 over six layers the six written layers take the divisors 3, 4, 5, 5, 4 and 3 -- `smin` supplies the -2 and -1 of the first two and nothing after, the select supplies the -1 and -2 of the last two and nothing before -- so the two edge terms are separated from each other as well as from the constant 5. Signedness is the whole point of the call: `t - 2r` is -2 and -1 as an i16, which an unsigned minimum (or a maximum) reads as a huge positive and answers 0, making the first two divisors 5 and leaving the other four unchanged. The six input values per column are chosen so that every one of the six window sums is an exact multiple of its own divisor and the six quotients are distinct: column 0 holds 1, 2, 3, 6, 18, 21 and answers 2, 3, 6, 10, 12, 15; column 1 holds 4, 9, 8, 11, 13, 24 and answers 7, 8, 9, 13, 14, 16. All twelve inputs and all twelve answers are distinct, so a layer permuted, a column swapped, a window that started or ended one layer off, or a divisor taken from the wrong step all land on a value no correct texel holds. Every quotient is a small integer and equals its own reciprocal-multiplied form in f32, so `fdiv fast` cannot separate the two spellings here. The four channels carry the same layer value scaled by 1, 3, 9 and -1, which makes each texel's components mutually distinct (so a swizzle shows) and puts a negative through the same divide. The destination starts as 0xBE poison in all 192 bytes. Note the shader's own loop runs one step past the last in-range layer and writes at array index `arraySize`; Metal discards a write outside a texture's bounds, and that discarded write is the shader's behaviour, not something this case chooses. `execution_safety` is `authored_bounded`: the AIR loop is a real cycle whose trip count is `arraySize + boxRadius + 1`, which this case pins to 9.","render_targets":[],"samplers":[],"stage":"kernel","texture_arrays":[],"textures":[{"binding":0,"bytes_b64":"AACAPwAAQEAAABBBAACAvwAAgEAAAEBBAAAQQgAAgMAAAABAAADAQAAAkEEAAADAAAAQQQAA2EEAAKJCAAAQwQAAQEAAABBBAADYQQAAQMAAAABBAADAQQAAkEIAAADBAADAQAAAkEEAAFhCAADAwAAAMEEAAARCAADGQgAAMMEAAJBBAABYQgAAIkMAAJDBAABQQQAAHEIAAOpCAABQwQAAqEEAAHxCAAA9QwAAqMEAAMBBAACQQgAAWEMAAMDB","dimensions":[2,1,6],"format":"rgba32_float","role":"input","texture_type":"d2_array"},{"binding":1,"dimensions":[2,1,6],"format":"rgba32_float","initial_bytes_b64":"vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+vr6+","role":"output","texture_type":"d2_array"}],"threadgroup_memory":[],"vertex_inputs":[],"visible_function_references":[],"visible_function_tables":[]}
